        "root_concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Demographic Dividend",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DIVIDEND 1 (Quantity effect):\n    More workers per dependent → more output per capita possible.\n    GDP per capita ≈ (GDP / Worker) × (Workers / Population)\n    Second term = labor force ratio = f(age structure)\n    When working-age bulge is large: workers/population ratio is maximized."
    },
    {
      "id": "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md#006",
      "path": [
        "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:demography:09-demographic-dividend, git-history:demography:09-demographic-dividend]",
        "canonical_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "current_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "id": "maxim:demography:demographic-dividend",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "demography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Demographic Dividend",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Bloom & Williamson (1998) estimate for East Asia:\n    ~1/3 of East Asian economic miracle (1965-1990) attributable to\n    favorable demographic structure.\n    GDP per capita growth: ~6.1% per year\n    Demographic contribution: ~1.5-2.0 percentage points"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md#007",
      "path": [
        "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:demography:09-demographic-dividend, git-history:demography:09-demographic-dividend]",
        "canonical_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "current_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "id": "maxim:demography:demographic-dividend",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "demography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Demographic Dividend",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DIVIDEND 2 (Behavior/savings effect):\n    Working-age adults have higher marginal savings rates than dependents.\n    Why? Life-cycle savings hypothesis (Modigliani):\n    Young workers save for retirement (positive saving)\n    Retired elderly dissave (spend down savings)\n    Children dependent (net consumers, not savers)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md#008",
      "path": [
        "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:demography:09-demographic-dividend, git-history:demography:09-demographic-dividend]",
        "canonical_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "current_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "id": "maxim:demography:demographic-dividend",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "demography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "section": "demography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Demographic Dividend",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "With large working-age cohort + small dependent cohort:\n    → National savings rate rises\n    → Investment capital accumulates\n    → Capital deepening → higher wages → more growth\n    → This is the economics/ Solow model connection: capital accumulation phase"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md#009",
      "path": [
        "09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:demography:09-demographic-dividend, git-history:demography:09-demographic-dividend]",
        "canonical_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "concepts": "[demographic, dividend]",
        "current_path": "demography/09-DEMOGRAPHIC-DIVIDEND.md",
        "id": "maxim:demography:demographic-dividend",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "demography",
