      },
      "text": "Key question: How much of growth was demographic?\n  Bloom & Williamson (1998): econometric analysis of 78 developing countries\n    Labor supply growth (from age structure) accounts for 1.37-1.87 percentage\n    points per year of East Asian growth rate premium over other regions\n    This explains ~1/3 of the 6% per year East Asia vs. 2% rest-of-world gap"
    },
