      "text": "MECHANISM IN DETAIL:\n  1. Fertility decline → youth dependency ratio falls\n  2. Large working cohort + small youth cohort → female labor force participation rises\n     (fewer children → women can work; daycare demand manageable)\n  3. Household savings rate rises (Modigliani lifecycle: workers save)\n  4. Government fiscal savings: fewer schools, pediatric health services needed\n  5. Private investment capital: domestic savings → investment → capital stock\n  6. Export orientation: large, low-wage (initially) labor force → manufacturing\n  7. Human capital: quality investment per child rises → education\n  All feeding into sustained 6-8% annual GDP growth for 30+ years\n```"
    },
    {
